stein</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Extended somatic support for pregnant women after brain death</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>1241</fpage><lpage>49</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12682499</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.CCM.0000059643.45027.96</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Appel</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Defining death: when physicians and family differ</article-title><source>J Med Ethics</source><year>2005</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>641</fpage><lpage>642</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16269560</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jme.2005.011718</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Machado</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A definition of human death should not be related to organ transplants</article-title><source>J Med Ethics</source><year>2003</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>202</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12796446</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jme.29.3.201</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jonas</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Jonas H</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Against the stream. Comments on the definition and redefinition of death</article-title><source>Philosophical essays: from ancient creed to technological man</source><year>1974</year><publisher-name>Prentice Hall, Englewood Cliffs, NJ</publisher-name><fpage>132</fpage><lpage>140</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Danish Council of Ethics</collab></person-group><article-title>Death Criteria: a report</article-title><source>The Danish Council of Ethics, Denmark</source><year>1988</year></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>